# =====================================================================
# Release V167 -- Billing.Invoice_Line_Adjustment (amend one line on one invoice)
# =====================================================================
# A recorded manual correction to ONE user's line on ONE month: drop it, or charge a different
# figure. The Admin screen writes it; usp_Generate_Invoice_Lines applies it last.
#
# ==> WHY NEITHER EXISTING ROUTE WORKS. <== Asked how to take a leaver off an invoice, the two
# obvious answers both fail:
#   * "Set them to No access on Subscriptions" -- does NOT remove the charge for the current month.
#     The generator bills from Security.Access_Log intervals and its rule is that mid-month changes
#     stay FULL month (pro-rata is sign-up only), so an access change stamped today still bills the
#     whole of this month. It only stops the next one.
#   * "Let the Dentally deactivation handle it" (V165) -- removes the row from
#     Security.Application_Users, which drops that user from EVERY month that is ever regenerated,
#     past ones included.
# Neither expresses "this user should not have been on THIS invoice". This table does.
#
# WHY NOT JUST EDIT Billing.Invoice_Line: it is DELETEd and rebuilt on every generation, and the
# billing run regenerates freely while a month is still a draft. A hand-edited line would revert
# silently, most likely between someone checking it and the invoice going out. Adjustments sit
# outside the rebuild and are re-applied every time.
#
# An 'override' with a NULL value is IGNORED rather than honoured -- a missing figure is a mistake,
# and billing nothing is not the safe reading of it. Reason and Created_By are stored because this
# changes what a practice is charged, and a bank statement will disagree with it months later.
#
# A month that already holds a FINALISED invoice is still protected: billing_run refuses to
# regenerate it, so an adjustment added after the fact does nothing until the invoice is credited.
# That is the intended order -- credit, then amend, then re-issue.
#
# Guarded CREATE + a proc redeploy, so idempotent and safe to re-run.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V167__invoice_line_adjustment.manifest
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Billing.Invoice_Line_Adjustment.Table.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Billing.usp_Generate_Invoice_Lines.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
